    "title": "Today’s NYT Connections hint & answers #1030: clues for April 6",
    "text": "Clues and hints to help you solve puzzle #1030 Updated: Apr 6, 2026 11:01 am WePC is reader-supported. When you buy through links on our site, we may earn an affiliate commission. Prices subject to change. Learn more Stuck on today’s NYT Connections puzzle? You’re in the right place. With 16 words split into four groups and only a few mistakes allowed, it’s easy to get tripped up. Some words seem like they belong in multiple groups, which makes things more confusing. This guide gives you helpful hints first, then the full answers if you need them. Below, you’ll find hints and answers to NYT Connections puzzle #1030, released on April 6. Hints for today’s Connections groups Here are four clues to help you sort today’s groups. They go from easiest to hardest: 🟨 hint: Boogie down 🟩 hint: A portion of a business or venture 🟦 hint: Popular arcade game 🟪 hint: Broadway, baby If you’d like an extra nudge, here’s one word from each group: 🟨: BALL 🟩: SHARE 🟦: MOLE 🟪: EVITE Today’s Connections answers (April 6) If you’re ready for the full solution, here it is: 🟨 Events with dancing: BALL, HOEDOWN, HOP, RAVE 🟩 Interest: CLAIM, CONCERN, SHARE, STAKE 🟦 Components of Whac-A-Mole: HOLES, MALLET, MOLE, TIMER 🟪 Musicals with last letter changed: CAROUSER, EVITE, OLIVES, WICKET Today’s puzzle leans toward medium difficulty. The yellow group was the easiest to spot, while the green group also made sense once you thought in business terms. The blue group required recognizing a specific game, and the purple group was the trickiest. That last set needed wordplay and some familiarity with musical titles to fully click. Does Connections get harder every day? Connections doesn’t get harder in a steady way. Some days are simple, while others depend heavily on niche knowledge or clever word tricks. Each puzzle uses a different style, from definitions to wordplay or cultural references. Once you solve one or two groups, the rest usually fall into place more easily.",
